    "theorem": "MillerLevelCompatibilityAudit.miller_level_compatibility_certificate",
    "statement": "theorem miller_level_compatibility_certificate : (∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [DecidableEq K] (W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine K) (_ : W.Δ ≠ 0) (P : W.Point) (n : ℕ) (_ : n • P = 0) (a : ℕ), millerFunction W P (a * n) = millerFunction W P n ^ a) ∧ (∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [DecidableEq K] (W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine K) (hΔ : W.Δ ≠ 0) (P : W.Point) (n N : ℕ) (hP : n • P = 0) (hN : n ∣ N) (D : W.Point →₀ ℤ) (hd : Disjoint D.support (functionDivisor W (millerUnit W P n) (millerUnit W P n).ne_zero).support), Disjoint D.support (functionDivisor W (millerUnit W P N) (millerUnit W P N).ne_zero).support ∧ evaluateDivisor W D (millerUnit W P N) (divisibleDomain W hΔ P n N hP hN D hd) = evaluateDivisor W D (millerUnit W P n) hd ^ (N / n)) ∧ (∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [DecidableEq K] (W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine K) (hΔ : W.Δ ≠ 0) (P : W.Point) (n N M : ℕ) (_ : 0 < n) (_ : 0 < N) (hP : n • P = 0) (hnN : n ∣ N) (_ : N ∣ M) (D : W.Point →₀ ℤ) (hd : Disjoint D.support (functionDivisor W (millerUnit W P n) (millerUnit W P n).ne_zero).support), evaluateDivisor W D (millerUnit W P N) (divisibleDomain W hΔ P n N hP hnN D hd) ^ (M / N) = evaluateDivisor W D (millerUnit W P n) hd ^ (M / n)) ∧ TestCurve.Δ ≠ 0 ∧ GeometricCurve.Δ ≠ 0 ∧ Fintype.card TestField = 5 ∧ Fintype.card TestField - 1 = 4 ∧ (2 : ℕ) ∣ 4 ∧ (4 : ℕ) ∣ Fintype.card TestField - 1 ∧ addOrderOf twoTorsionPoint = 2 ∧ (2 : ℕ) • twoTorsionPoint = 0 ∧ addOrderOf basePoint = 3 ∧ (2 : ℕ) • basePoint ≠ 0 ∧ TestCurve.Nonsingular (2 : TestField) 3 ∧ divisorDegree TestCurve positiveDivisor = 0 ∧ divisorDegree TestCurve negativeDivisor = 0 ∧ divisorDegree GeometricCurve (geometricDifference basePoint safePoint) = 0 ∧ divisorDegree GeometricCurve (geometricDifference point23 twoTorsionPoint) = 0 ∧ Disjoint (geometricDifference basePoint safePoint).support (functionDivisor GeometricCurve (levelGeometricFunction twoTorsionPoint 2) (level_geometric_nonzero twoTorsionPoint 2)).support ∧ Disjoint (geometricDifference basePoint safePoint).support (functionDivisor GeometricCurve (levelGeometricFunction twoTorsionPoint 4) (level_geometric_nonzero twoTorsionPoint 4)).support ∧ Disjoint (geometricDifference point23 twoTorsionPoint).support (functionDivisor GeometricCurve (levelGeometricFunction basePoint 2) (level_geometric_nonzero basePoint 2)).support ∧ Disjoint (geometricDifference point23 twoTorsionPoint).support (functionDivisor GeometricCurve (levelGeometricFunction basePoint 4) (level_geometric_nonzero basePoint 4)).support ∧ millerFunction TestCurve basePoint 4 ≠ millerFunction TestCurve basePoint 2 ^ 2 ∧ (evaluateDivisor TestCurve positiveDivisor (millerUnit TestCurve twoTorsionPoint 2) positive_domain_two : TestField) = 2 ∧ (evaluateDivisor TestCurve positiveDivisor (millerUnit TestCurve twoTorsionPoint 4) positive_domain_four : TestField) = 4 ∧ (evaluateDivisor TestCurve negativeDivisor (millerUnit TestCurve basePoint 2) negative_domain_two : TestField) = 1 ∧ (evaluateDivisor TestCurve negativeDivisor (millerUnit TestCurve basePoint 4) negative_domain_four : TestField) = 3 ∧ (evaluateDivisor TestCurve positiveDivisor (millerUnit TestCurve twoTorsionPoint 2) positive_domain_two : TestField) ^ (4 / 2 : ℕ) = (evaluateDivisor TestCurve positiveDivisor (millerUnit TestCurve twoTorsionPoint 4) positive_domain_four : TestField) ^ (4 / 4 : ℕ) ∧ (evaluateDivisor TestCurve negativeDivisor (millerUnit TestCurve basePoint 2) negative_domain_two : TestField) ^ (4 / 2 : ℕ) ≠ (evaluateDivisor TestCurve negativeDivisor (millerUnit TestCurve basePoint 4) negative_domain_four : TestField) ^ (4 / 4 : ℕ) ∧ (4 : TestField) ≠ 1",
    "decl_sha256": "6a6628b9f2c6a3727ac4069803840c6f68da4702658b03d1f34ac7595f00e8cf",
    "scope": "Actual chosen Miller-function and guarded final-evaluation core of Galbraith Exercise26.3.8. For every FieldK/actual DecidableEqK/actual WΔneq0/allcharacteristics, actual nP=0 implies chosen f_(a*n)=f_n^a, including explicit zero/one extensions. For n|N, actual lower final principal-support disjointness derives actual higher final domain; actual local-unit divisor evaluation gives f_N(D)=f_n(D)^(N/n), with no supplied correctness/commutation premise. For positive n,N and n|N|M, actual final exponents M/N and M/n agree. This is a function/evaluation core, not construction of canonical Tate or representative independence. Actual F5 E:y²=x³+1, n2/N4/M4/cardK5/nonzero discriminant. Positive P=(4,0)exactorder2, D=(0,1)−(2,2), degree0/fullactualAC(F5) final domains at both levels: proper values2/4/final4=4neq1. Negative P=(0,1)exactorder3/not2torsion, D=(2,3)−(4,0), same n/N/M and proper fullgeometric final domains: values1/3/final1neq3. Actual f4neqf2² via actual point orders0vs−2 at(0,4). Source qualified torsion-domain function/evaluation compatibility survives; deleting its actual first-argument torsion guard fails. No claim that source omitted its pairing domain. Six new modules and87frozen local dependency modules/0copies, all90dependency formal/config sources pinned and all107predecessor formal/artifactpins checked before/after every build. Fresh new-project alltracked theorem/transitiveaxiom gate distinct from credited predecessor679. Default limits/standard foundations. Original Miller paper unread; no novelty/physicalhost/backend/runtime/signedstanding/canonicalpromotion/full14 claim. Scheme/divisorbasechange/descent/translation/reciprocity/isogeny/Lang/Cartier/Jacobian/canonicalWeilTate/MOVFR/remaining14 stayopen. No frozen edits/cryptographic Python/paidcompute/agentupload.",
